I'm making an emotional appeal before my logical brain has the chance to 
shut me up.

This is honestly and earnestly how I feel. I don't have the ability to 
block people or delete comments on the mailing list, but I will not even 
think twice about ignoring everything you post ever again and completely 
writing you off as a person if you post some kind of inflammatory response. 
It has now reached the point where I almost dread trying to catch up on the 
mailing list each day. I'm now ignoring entire threads because they 
degenerate into "well, if you accept *this* proposal..." and "If you use 
X's interpretation..." and post after post of unhelpful argument that 
seriously causes me stress just to see existing. I will try to say this as 
few times and as clearly as possible.

*If you are not working on the CLL, creating media in or translating media 
to Lojban, filling gaps in the vocabulary, teaching classes, or actually 
learning the language, you are working against our progress and working 
directly against the people that have put in countless hours to actually 
help us meet our goals. You are expending effort that is useless to us and 
I personally do not want you as part of our community. You create 
disharmony, you create distractions to everybody, and I need you to stop 
it. I need absolutely everybody in the community to one of those five 
things or take your business elsewhere for when it's not a detriment to our 
community.*

If you have an issue/problem/proposal/suggestion, it can be addressed to 
the BPFK either by the website's BPFK proposals/issues section, or by the 
mailing list, and it will be archived to be examined only when we've 
finished the new CLL and the dictionary. It will not be regarded or 
considered until then.

I'm trying to appeal to you as a person you know, a member of your 
community, and as somebody that has put actual serious time and effort 
numbering nearly or over a thousand hours into helping the BPFK and LLG. 
This is causing me serious stress and has, due to me cutting off lots of 
ties and contacts that were hurting and hindering me, now become one of the 
top five sources of health-hindering and life-hindering stress in my life. 
How terrible is it that one of your top five greatest joys in life is also 
one of your top five causes of pain? I'm at the point where I have 
absolutely no tolerance, so we can come together and put in one big effort 
to grow as  a community, or you can keep doing what you're doing and not 
have me around any more. This is not a threat, it's just an IF/THEN.

(This rage-post does not necessarily reflect the opinions/views of the LLG, 
its members, or any subcommittee thereof. This is entirely personal in 
nature and should be read at face-value. Constructive comments and 
criticisms are welcome; inflammatory/defensive/angry responses and their 
posters will be written off and ignored.)

